  "fits": [
    {
      "fact": "Made for 45 cm rimless tanks (UNS 45) with glass no thicker than 5 mm",
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "fact": "The legs have a fixed width, so it only fits the tank size it was made for. If you may upgrade tanks, the EA version has adjustable legs",
      "source": 1
    },
    {
      "fact": "Mid-range output, brighter than the C and B lines but weaker than the S line. It suits low-tech to high-tech tanks and a wide range of plants",
      "source": 1
    },
    {
      "fact": "Demanding plants such as red stem plants are better served by the S or SA series",
      "source": 1
    },
    {
      "fact": "For a 450E paired with a 45 × 35 × 30 cm tank, the Korean brand site gives a maximum tank width of about 50 cm (this refers to the current E Line)",
      "source": 4
    },
    {
      "fact": "The 450EA IV sibling is not waterproof. It is meant for open-top tanks, hung at least 6 inches above the water, and not inside a hood or lid",
      "source": 2
    }
  ],
  "usage": [
    {
      "fact": "Installs by resting the fixed legs on the glass edges of a rimless tank",
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "fact": "Brightness is set with the inline dimmer that comes in the box",
      "source": 1
    },
    {
      "fact": "The EA IV sibling's inline controller has on/off, a sunrise/sunset ramp, a 7-step dimmer and a timer",
      "source": 2
    },
    {
      "fact": "Includes a power supply and brackets. EU-plug units need an adapter in other markets",
      "source": 2
    }
  ],
  "issues": [
    {
      "fact": "Version IV has been replaced by E Line V. The V version has six colour channels, Bluetooth app control (LightControl Pro) and legs that extend up to 4 inches per side. Version IV has fixed legs and only the inline dimmer",
      "source": 1
    },
    {
      "fact": "The 450E V is rated at 31 W and 2100 lm, compared with 28 W and 1850 lm for the 450E IV",
      "source": 9
    },
    {
      "fact": "Stock of version IV is limited: one US retailer lists it only for pre-order",
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "fact": "Retailers mix up the E and EA names. One shop titles its page '450E IV' but lists 450EA specs (30 W, 1500 lm), so check the model code before buying",
      "source": 2
    },
    {
      "fact": "No Vietnamese shop website lists the 450E IV. Brothers Concept has only 600ES and 900ES (out of stock), and Vuaqua lists an ES 600E as 'Liên hệ' (call for price)",
      "source": 8
    }
  ],
  "alternatives": [
